      "content": "6.1 National Leaders from Kerala"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Sir C. Sankaran Nair was the only Keralite to serve as the President of the Indian National Congress.",
        "V.K. Krishna Menon served as India's Defence Minister and was a pivotal diplomat in shaping India's non-aligned foreign policy.",
        "Kerala's prominent scientists and technocrats have played crucial roles in space research, atomic energy, and national development.",
        "Kerala's pioneer leaders established historic precedents, including the first democratically elected communist government in 1957."
